# n8n Forms Pipeline

Migrating the booking pipeline's form backend from Basin to Sygnal Studio Forms
without breaking the n8n workflow that sits behind it. This doc tracks what we
know, what we've verified, and what's still to do.

## The live pipeline (verified 2026-11-20)

Three layers. The n8n call is **server-side, made by Basin** — it never appears
in page source, which is why it looked absent from the site.

1. **Browser → Basin.** `index.js` intercepts `#booking-form` and POSTs
   `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` to `usebasin.com/f/57139b8e2264`.
   The commented-out `webhook-test` script tag on the tour pages is a dead
   leftover (see REVIEW.hd) and plays no part.
2. **Basin → n8n.** Basin's webhook integration POSTs **JSON** (signed with
   `x-basin-signature`, UA `Faraday`) to the production webhook
   `http://sygnal-n8n-u1282.vm.elestio.app:5678/webhook/30647a93-a17d-4510-9d44-348f19252204`.
   Body = form fields + Basin metadata (below).
3. **n8n Webhook node** wraps each request as
   `{headers, params, query, body, webhookUrl, executionMode}` — this envelope
   is the node's own output format, nobody sends it. Downstream nodes read
   `$json.body.*`.

### Workflow shape (export: `n8n-workflow.json`, analysed 2026-11-20)

Webhook (POST, CORS `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`) fans out to:

- **Tour-Aid**: Set → HTTP Request (POST multipart to
  `https://navi.co.nz/tours/bookEnglishTours.php`, does an email
  notification; `continueOnFail`) → Sygnal Monitor (GET
  `https://monitor.sygnal.com/…/ping`)
- **Google Sheets Reporting**: Set1 → Append row in sheet (autoMapInputData;
  columns Tms, Name, Phone, Email, Tour-Code, Date, Adults, Children,
  Pick-Up, Arrival-Date, Departure-Date, Type, Notes)
- Disconnected: SPAM Check (POST `api.apilayer.com/spamchecker`, reads
  `body.name` / `body.email` / `body.notes`), "Record in Slack" section

Instances: original `sygnal-n8n-u1282` (production webhook target) and working
clone `sygnal-n8n-clone-u1282`. Reference execution: workflow
`68w9Rtxp2AXoerQp`, execution `14992` (on the clone).

**The contract: only the 19 flat `body.*` form/JS fields are consumed.**
`Set` and `Set1` read: `booking-type`, `date`, `notes`, `name`, `phone`,
`email`, `arrival-date`, `departure-date`, `terms-accepted`, `tour-code`,
`pick-up`, `tour`, `adults`, `children`, `total`, `totalFees`,
`totalWithFees`, `totalAdults`, `totalChildren`. **None of Basin's 13
metadata keys are referenced anywhere** — so the Studio payload only has to
deliver those 19 fields flat under `body`, nothing more.

Two incidental findings from the export:

- The Webhook node's `pinData` sample is a **browser-direct** urlencoded POST
  from `navi-tours.webflow.io` — the original integration had the page post
  straight to n8n (hence the CORS header). Basin forwarding (JSON) came
  later; n8n parses both encodings into `body.*` identically, so both shapes
  worked.
- Minor latent oddity: one Set field is named `=totalFees` (expression-mode
  name). It evaluates to `totalFees`, so it works, but it will confuse
  anyone editing the node.

### Payload body — field inventory

**Form fields** (browser-sent; ported form verified field-identical to live):
`date`, `booking-type`, `adults`, `children`, `notes`, `pick-up`, `name`,
`phone`, `email`, `arrival-date`, `departure-date`, `tour` (hidden),
`tour-code` (hidden), `terms-accepted`, `test` (leftover hidden field, always
`123` — present in the Webflow markup, carried into every submission).

**JS-appended at submit** (by the `index.js` intercept): `total`, `totalFees`,
`totalWithFees`, `totalAdults`, `totalChildren`.

**Basin-added metadata** (13 keys): `ip`, `geocoded_country`,
`geocoded_region`, `geocoded_city`, `timestamp`, `spam`, `spam_reason`, `id`,
`form_id`, `form_name`, `project_name`, `origin`, `attachments`.

## The question to answer

When a Studio form fires its outbound webhook at the same n8n endpoint, does
its JSON body match the Basin shape — or do we add a transform step (or shape
Studio's payload) so `$json.body.*` references keep resolving?

Known risk areas:

- **Nesting** — Studio stores submission fields in a `data` object; if the
  webhook mirrors that, every flat `$json.body.X` reference breaks.
- **Metadata naming** — Studio: `country`/`city`, `spam_score`/`signals`.
  Basin: `geocoded_*`, `spam`/`spam_reason`, plus `id`/`form_id`/`form_name`/
  `project_name` with no obvious Studio twins.
- **Encoding** — Basin sends JSON; confirm what Studio sends.

## Constraints hit so far

- The `n8n-mcp` server in `.mcp.json` fails to load (cause unknown; endpoint
  is plain `http://` :5678 — may need an auth header).
- DevTools-driven Chrome is blocked at the clone's n8n sign-in, so workflow
  export and execution reads need the PM's own browser session.
- The Studio Forms MCP exposes **no webhook configuration** on forms or sites
  (checked both schemas 2026-11-20) — webhook targets are set elsewhere
  (Studio UI).

## The catcher (in place, 2026-11-20)

Instead of a catcher workflow in n8n, the dev site itself catches: dev-only
Astro route `web/src/pages/api/webhook-capture.ts`.

- `POST /api/webhook-capture` — records method, headers, raw body, and the
  body parsed as JSON or urlencoded. This is the URL Studio's webhook targets
  (through the tunnel).
- `GET /api/webhook-capture` — lists captures; `?clear=1` empties.
- Captures live in module memory (dev SSR runs in workerd; its filesystem is
  virtual, so no disk) — **read back promptly after each submission**, an HMR
  reload clears them.
- Self-tested with JSON and urlencoded POSTs; answers 404 when deployed.
  Delete the route when this investigation closes.

Studio prod form for the test: **Booking Form**, muid `GwaxVWaQb0a7`
(site Navi `Ho6HGiKgfFh3`, account 72). Webhook target must be configured in
the Studio UI (the MCP has no webhook surface).

